WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
What makes life painful in a way it is not for cats and dogs is that we can think.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
We ask: Why am I alive? Where did I come from, and where am I going?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
This series will explore more difficult questions. I will leave them aside today.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Many thinkers, philosophers and scholars throughout history have studied this.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Human wisdom asks human questions, and human knowledge searches for answers.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.000
In the end, none of it gives us a sure foundation for life.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:58.000
But there is One who created us, explains us, and tells us where we came from.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.000
The greatest thing is that He has spoken.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
If He had not spoken, it would remain a mystery.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Imagine someone standing here for half an hour, saying and singing nothing. We could not bear it; it would be too mysterious.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:29.000
If I stood here without saying a word, you would think this gathering made no sense—like a mysterious silent play.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Without a word, the universe, life and everything in it would be a silent mystery.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:45.000
But the Bible tells us that God is real and living, and that He has spoken.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.000
God’s word says again and again, “This is what I have said.”

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:58.000
He says, “Heaven and earth will pass away, but not the smallest stroke of my words. My word is established in heaven and never changes.”
